# Firebase web config for the GrimeLine project.
#
# These six values are committed on purpose. A Firebase web config is not a
# secret — it ships inside the JavaScript bundle of every Firebase web app by
# design, and Google documents it as safe to include in source. It identifies
# the project; it does not grant access to it.
#
# What actually protects the data:
#   - firestore.rules / storage.rules, which allow only the two crew uids
#   - Firebase Auth → Authorised domains, which limits where sign-in works
#
# Committing them removes a whole class of deployment failure: a build that
# succeeds, serves a "not configured" screen, and looks broken. Anything set in
# Vercel's environment variables still overrides these, so switching projects
# later needs no code change.
#
# The Map ID is here for the same reason: it is a style identifier that rides
# along in every tile request. It is not a credential and grants nothing.
#
# Deliberately NOT here:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY — billable and abused if scraped. Set it in
#     Vercel and restrict it by HTTP referrer in Google Cloud.
#   Anything server-side (Twilio, Meta, the service-account key, CRON_SECRET).
#     Those are real secrets and must never be committed.

NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSyBbfjOLni6RfEIHS3Z9nBB_-Fe7GjpMhgk
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=grimeline-5e3d8.firebaseapp.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=grimeline-5e3d8
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=grimeline-5e3d8.firebasestorage.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=539472716244
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:539472716244:web:988ebb2c4703f31fcaf641
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_MAP_ID=17bcb51d93b8f9baf97cea97
